# Git worktrees. `.worktrees/` is where they used to live; the Claude Code
# harness puts them under `.claude/` instead, and that path was ignored by
# nothing — 15 GB of full repo checkouts, each with its own .git, one
# `git add -A` away from being committed. It is also why eslint reported 900
# parsing errors from the main checkout and why runAsserts skips the directory.
.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/

# Machine-local Claude Code settings: a per-machine permission allowlist, which
# is what the `.local` suffix means. `.claude/launch.json` is deliberately NOT
# ignored — it describes how to start this project's dev servers, which is the
# same for everyone working on it.
.claude/settings.local.json
